  "articleBody": "Painting interior walls sounds straightforward, but achieving smooth, durable coverage across an entire room requires a structured approach.\n\nOverview: Wall painting demands proper drywall prep, correct primer selection, and controlled roller technique for a clean, consistent sheen.\n\nKey Benefits: Quality wall painting resists scuffs, handles cleaning, and hides previous colors without flashing or visible lap marks.\n\nProcess Breakdown:\n- Surface Repair: Patch nail holes, settle cracks, and feather the edges smooth so patches do not show under room lighting.\n- Strategic Priming: Spot-prime patched areas and use stain-blocking primer over marks to prevent uneven paint absorption known as flashing.\n- Edge Cutting and Rolling: Cut along ceilings, trim, and corners with an angled brush, then roll adjacent sections with steady, even pressure while maintaining a wet edge.\n\nReal Examples: Homeowners often rush to roll walls without priming patched spackle, leaving dull, chalky spots across the room once the paint dries.\n\nQuestions to Ask Before You Decide: Ask your painter whether they patch and sand drywall imperfections, which paint line they use, and how they protect floors and trim during application.\n\nTo schedule your interior wall painting project, call Abraham Becerra at HH Remodeling LLC at 303-505-0866 to get started with an experienced finish contractor.",
  "datePublished": "2026-10-23"
